{
  "_comment": [
    "WRITTEN-DOWN ANSWERS FROM api.github.com, so the suite needs neither network nor git history.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The first version of authority-scope.test.mjs answered its API from the local git",
    "object store (`git ls-tree`, `git merge-base`). That is fatal in CI: both jobs that run this suite check",
    "out with actions/checkout at its default fetch-depth: 1, so commits 9f0131a, a51c8490 and 6feac016 are not",
    "objects in the clone, four tests died with `fatal: Not a valid commit name`, and the emit job failed before",
    "the emitter ran. An independent review caught it as a blocker.",
    "",
    "The ids here are real and were re-taken from the API by hand; the module's own header says the decision a",
    "run makes from GitHub's answers can be made in a test from written-down answers, and that the two are the",
    "same code. What a written-down answer must never do is stand in for a fact nobody checked - each entry below",
    "was observed, not composed.",
    "",
    "TAKEN: 2026-09-23, for BAWES-Universe/studenthub-platform, at",
    "  authority 9f0131a5df8687deccd1ac0c0b0dc08f9a3a689b  (the commit PR #163 landed as)",
    "  base      a51c8490dfb8572917049b3ab73dcf94409365c4  (its parent: the merge base of authority and candidate)",
    "  candidate 6feac016e3a0796d0c7b21d86426af0f1491a9c1 (the candidate the first dispatch on main refused)",
    "",
    "The two protected-side ids match what the refused run itself printed (3615f658... for the workflow file,",
    "03fe40ba... for the directory), which is why they are asserted verbatim in the tests."
  ],
